{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1786659693755409001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"stealthy-appetizing-coelacanth","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"14dfba506db8655465e8e4949b3a41cd50f9b9dbf3484bd4cc895cb2be83ea28","event_uuid":"20c1b6f2-e513-4484-9200-1866f779514a","position":{"commit_sha":"2420d8b34933a1c724c46013e0fe9a05efe2cebb","position":"1786652685862516001-20c1b6f2-e513-4484-9200-1866f779514a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"724662bc333019b0fc5a4209e61cd5d2f14ee296ea9329c0804485aaa32cbe25","event_uuid":"1cbb205a-8cf6-4980-84bd-00b2100ee654","position":{"commit_sha":"170e13fbafc823b04acc844628e2d984cef9fa0f","position":"1786652700022864001-1cbb205a-8cf6-4980-84bd-00b2100ee654"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786652685862516001,"creation_channel":"python","deps":[{"link_uuid":"1cbb205a-8cf6-4980-84bd-00b2100ee654","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"5e53-234f-5c65-477d"}],"description":"## The file\n\n`src/rebar/signing.py` is 798 LOC against the 800 hard cap — two lines of headroom. Deferred\nfrom `cinderlike-lucky-akitainu` (which took `pass1.py` and `_store/push.py` instead) because\nthis one cut cannot be made without editing a test, a different risk profile from those two.\n\n## Concern map (measured on origin/main @ 2af5a4c773)\n\n| concern | LOC | symbols |\n|---|---|---|\n| A manifest vocabulary + gate provenance | 158 | `SigningError`, `parse_manifest`, `VERIFIED_AT_SHA_PREFIX`, `verified_at_sha_step`, `verified_at_sha_from_manifest`, `verified_at_sha_subject`, `REBAR_VERSION_PREFIX`, `rebar_version_step`, `rebar_version_from_manifest`, `_gate_source_dir`, `_baked_commit_sha`, `_gate_commit_sha`, `gate_code_version`, `head_sha` |\n| B legacy symmetric HMAC scheme | 231 | `ALGORITHM`, `PAYLOAD_VERSION`, `_NO_KEY`, `signing_key`, `_generate_key_file`, `key_fingerprint`, `_canonical_payload`, `compute_signature`, `verify_record`, `_hmac_opcert_not_certified` |\n| C CLI arms | 103 | `sign_cli`, `verify_signature_cli` |\n| D dispatch + sign/verify paths | 194 | `OPCERT_KINDS`, `verify_attestation_record`, `_sign_manifest_under_lock`, `sign_manifest`, `_resolve_and_reduce`, `most_recent_attestation`, `_record_for_kind`, `verify_signature`, `verify_attestations` |\n\nProposed: sibling modules (NOT a package — the cap is per-file either way, and\n`_opcert_signing.py` is the established precedent, split out of this same module in story 8d8e).\n`_signing_manifest.py` ~198, `_signing_hmac.py` ~276, `signing.py` ~377. Direction\n`signing -> _signing_hmac -> _signing_manifest`, acyclic. An optional third cut\n(`_signing_cli.py` ~133) would take `signing.py` to ~245 but requires the CLI arms to import\n`rebar.signing` IN-FUNCTION, never at module level, or the eight `verify_signature` and one\n`sign_manifest` monkeypatches bind pre-patch and silently no-op.\n\n## Why it needs a test edit — the blocker\n\n`_baked_commit_sha` is monkeypatched on the `signing` module at `test_attestation_signing.py:139,151,162`,\nand its consumer `_gate_commit_sha` calls it as a BARE GLOBAL in the same file (`:308,:312`).\nMove both into `_signing_manifest.py` and `_gate_commit_sha` resolves `_baked_commit_sha` from\n`_signing_manifest.__dict__`, so the patch becomes a NO-OP. Two of the three tests fail loudly;\n`:162` (`assert \"STALEBAKED\" not in got`) passes VACUOUSLY — it silently stops testing the\nlive-over-baked precedence it was written to prove. That third one is the dangerous one.\n\nRemedies, in order: (1) re-point the three patches at\n`\"rebar._signing_manifest._baked_commit_sha\"` — legitimate, the symbol is private with zero src\nconsumers outside the family; (2) keep the whole gate-provenance sub-family (69 LOC) in\n`signing.py`, costing ~69 LOC on the entry module and shrinking `_signing_manifest.py` to ~129;\n(3) NOT an in-function `from rebar.signing import _baked_commit_sha` — that is a back-edge and\na cycle.\n\n## Other constraints found\n\n- `docs/reuse-surface.md` documents `sign_manifest`, `verify_signature`, `verify_attestations`,\n  `verify_record`, `head_sha`; `tests/unit/test_reuse_surface_doc.py` introspects NINE\n  `signing.*` callables with `inspect.signature`. Six of the nine move — the re-export must\n  carry them with unchanged parameter lists. That test is the CI tripwire.\n- Six PRIVATE names must be re-exported despite the underscore: `_gate_commit_sha` (imported by\n  `llm/build_drift.py:127`), `_baked_commit_sha`, `_NO_KEY`, `_generate_key_file`,\n  `_canonical_payload`, `_hmac_opcert_not_certified`.\n- Silent-behaviour flag: `verify_record` and `_hmac_opcert_not_certified` call\n  `verified_at_sha_from_manifest` / `rebar_version_from_manifest` as bare globals. After the cut\n  they resolve in `_signing_hmac`'s globals, so a patch on `signing` no longer reaches them. No\n  test depends on that today, but it is a real semantic change and should be stated in the\n  commit.\n- `.github/complexity-baseline.json` has ZERO keys for `signing.py` — the `--lock` gate is not a\n  constraint here.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `signing.py` <= 500 LOC; every new module in [100, 500].\n- [ ] All nine `signing.*` callables in `test_reuse_surface_doc.py` reachable with unchanged\n      signatures; the six private names re-exported.\n- [ ] The `_baked_commit_sha` hazard resolved by remedy (1) or (2), stated explicitly, with the\n      `:162` vacuous-pass risk addressed rather than left latent.\n- [ ] Full-suite test-count parity; `make lint`, `make typecheck`, module-size contract green.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"f5c1-e41d-33b7-4c7b","ticket_type":"story","title":"Split signing.py (798 LOC, two lines from the cap) by concern","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["20c1b6f2-e513-4484-9200-1866f779514a","1cbb205a-8cf6-4980-84bd-00b2100ee654"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786659693755409001,"uuid":"4298d739-187d-4841-95f4-afa2c6f08973"}